Ladybird sizes an input with a table display the way it sizes the
input with the display a replaced element uses for it, block or
inline, and builds its box for that display. Blink’s LayoutTheme::
AdjustStyle() computes “display: table” on such a control as block and
every other table display as inline-block, and WebKit’s RenderTheme::
adjustStyle() does the same. Gecko keeps the computed value, but
nsCSSFrameConstructor:: FindElementTagData() picks the frame of an
input in FindInputData() before FindDisplayData() reads its display,
so no table display can make an input a table part. Run in Chrome
157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5: Each submit, button,
reset, file, and color input in the test has the same size under every
table display as under “display: block”.
